panfrost: push UBO 0 only when it is the GL default block (AIR shaders have none).

pan_shader.c asserted s->info.first_ubo_is_default_ubo before making UBO 0
pushable. Metal's buffers come out of the AIR frontend as ordinary constant
buffers, with no default block (rusticl's kernels are the same until it lowers
their inputs and sets the flag), so with asserts on -- our phone build is
debugoptimized with b_ndebug=false -- every AIR fragment shader and kernel
aborted in panfrost_shader_compile. Found 11-28 on the PC: host air_run built
against panfrost under Mesa's noop drm-shim with PAN_GPU_ID=6000 (Mali-G71)
aborted on both phase 2 tests (AppleMetalGLRenderer clearFragment01, AV1SW
BlitLumaKernel_Uint). Now UBO 0 is pushable only when it is the default
block; every other UBO load goes through the UBO descriptors, which panfrost
fills for every bound constant buffer (always correct, never pushed). GL
shaders keep exactly the old behaviour.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_shader.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_shader.c
@@ -200,8 +200,11 @@
     * present). Both of these are mapped on the CPU, but other UBOs are not.
     * When we switch to pushing UBOs with a compute kernel (or CSF instructions)
     * we can relax this. */
-   assert(s->info.first_ubo_is_default_ubo);
-   inputs.pushable_ubos = BITFIELD_BIT(0);
+   /* AIR (Metal) shaders, like rusticl's before it lowers its kernel inputs,
+    * come with no default UBO: Metal's buffers are ordinary constant buffers,
+    * so UBO 0 is pushed only when it is the GL default block, and every other
+    * UBO load goes through the UBO descriptors (always correct, never pushed). */
+   inputs.pushable_ubos = s->info.first_ubo_is_default_ubo ? BITFIELD_BIT(0) : 0;
 
    if (out->sysvals.sysval_count != 0) {
       unsigned sysval_ubo = s->info.num_ubos - 1;
